{
  "name": "551. A custom provider's video id names it, so retrieve and download reach it with its own key (custom provider video ids) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7085 (Codex P1 on #221). A custom provider on the replicate, volcengine or modelark base reports its own name since TXE-7085, and the video ids it returns carry that name (`<id>:<custom provider>`). The gateway routes a retrieve, download or delete by that suffix, so the call reaches the custom provider, with its own key and base_url. Before, the ids carried the base's suffix (`:replicate`, `:volcengine`, `:modelark`) and those calls went to the built-in provider. The custom providers are the folder-485 ones (tkp_ovr_<base>, base_url /pp/ovr/<base> on the provider error fixture); the fixture answers their default video paths for one prediction (pred_ovr_video) and one Ark task (cgt-ovr-video) and records every call with the name of the key it carried. Replicate serves create and retrieve only; volcengine and modelark also download. An id with the legacy base suffix is routed by the gateway to the built-in provider, so its handling in the custom provider (providerUtils.StripVideoIDProviderSuffixOrBase) is reachable only through the Go SDK and is pinned by Go tests. Red before this change: each create returns the base's suffix.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[NO-CONTENT] tkp_ovr_replicate video create: POST /v1/videos returns an id that names tkp_ovr_replicate (custom provider video ids)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "tk-key-ovr-replicate"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"model\":\"tkp_ovr_replicate/fixture/ovr-video\",\"prompt\":\"a cat on a mat\",\"seconds\":\"4\"}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/videos",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "videos"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('custom provider video ids setup: the fixture was reset', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200);",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var body = {}; try { body = pm.response.json() || {}; } catch (e) { body = {}; }",
              "pm.test('the video was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "pm.test('its id names the custom provider, so a later call is routed back to it (before TXE-7085: :replicate)', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(body.id, pm.response.text()).to.equal('pred_ovr_video:tkp_ovr_replicate');",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('cpv_replicate_id', body.id || '');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__wire', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture answered /__wire', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "  var calls = res.json().data[0].calls.filter(function (c) { return c.path.indexOf('/pp/ovr/') === 0; });",
              "  pm.test('one call reached the custom provider\\'s upstream: POST /pp/ovr/replicate/v1/models/fixture/ovr-video/predictions', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(calls.map(function (c) { return c.method + ' ' + c.path; }), JSON.stringify(calls)).to.eql(['POST /pp/ovr/replicate/v1/models/fixture/ovr-video/predictions']);",
              "  });",
              "  pm.test('it carried the custom provider\\'s key tk-key-ovr-replicate', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(calls.map(function (c) { return c.key; }), JSON.stringify(calls)).to.eql(['tk-key-ovr-replicate']);",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
